# Copy to am_plr/mcp/.env (git-ignored) and fill in what you need.
#
# Setup writes these values literally into the generated am_plr/.mcp.json, so Claude Code does not
# need them in its own environment. A variable left empty (or commented out) here is OMITTED from
# .mcp.json, and the server falls back to its own .env - which is how qase already works.
#
# Which server reads what:
#   teamcity         TEAMCITY_TOKEN      nothing else provides it - fill this one in
#   qase             QASE_API_TOKEN      optional: vso-engine-autotests/.env already has it
#   victoriametrics  VICTORIAMETRICS_URL optional, no auth (the default URL works on the VPN)
#   cats-mcp-server  -                   no credentials
#   asana            -                   SSE, you authorise it in Claude Code
#
# The optional ones are marked ${VAR?} in upstreams.toml, so setup reports them instead of warning.

TEAMCITY_TOKEN=

# QASE_API_TOKEN=
# VICTORIAMETRICS_URL=
